---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AnswerBox from '../components/AnswerBox.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';

const path = '/our-guarantee/';

/* Keystone doctrine #6: the guarantee is a DEFINED TERM linked from every
   use of the word, never an open-ended promise. The old /guarantee/ page had
   the right content but marked its T&C subsections as H2s rather than H3s
   under a terms parent — fixed here. */
const answer =
  'Our 100% Service Guarantee means that if covered pests return between scheduled visits on an active program, we come back and re-service at no additional charge. It is a defined re-service commitment, not an open-ended promise, and the conditions that apply are listed in full on this page.';

const terms = [
  ['Satisfaction', 'If pests covered by your program return between scheduled visits, we return and re-service at no additional charge for the balance of the program period.'],
  ['Customer cooperation', 'Re-service depends on reasonable access to the treated areas and on the preparation steps we provide before a visit. Where preparation has not been completed, we will reschedule rather than treat.'],
  ['Materials', 'We use materials registered for the site and the target pest and apply them according to the label. Label directions govern where a label and a request conflict.'],
  ['Insurance', 'We carry general liability insurance. Certificates are available on request for commercial accounts and property managers.'],
  ['A change in law', 'If a change in law or label restricts a material or method we relied on, we will substitute an equivalent approach and tell you what changed.'],
  ['Pest damage', 'This is a service guarantee covering re-treatment. It is not a warranty against structural or property damage caused by pests.'],
  ['Rodent control placement', 'Rodent devices are placed where they are effective and where they can be serviced safely. Placement is our decision, and we will explain it.'],
  ['Non-payment and default', 'Guarantee coverage pauses on an account that is past due and resumes when the balance is cleared.'],
  ['Cancellation', 'Recurring programs can be canceled. There is no long-term contract, and the notice period and any remaining balance are set out in your service agreement.'],
];
---
<BaseLayout
  path={path}
  title="Our 100% Service Guarantee"
  description="What the Sasquatch Pest Control 100% Service Guarantee covers, what it does not, and the full terms and conditions that apply to every treatment we perform."
  kind="page"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Guarantee', path }]}
>
  <h1>Our 100% Service Guarantee</h1>
  <AnswerBox text={answer} />

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What the guarantee means for you</h2>
    <p>
      A guarantee is only worth what its terms say. Ours is a re-service
      commitment with defined conditions, published in full below, so you can
      read exactly what you are getting before you buy rather than after.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does not mean</h2>
    <p>
      This is the part most guarantee pages leave out, and leaving it out is what
      makes a guarantee worthless. Ours is a commitment to come back and
      re-service. It is not a promise that you will never see another insect, it
      is not a warranty against structural or property damage caused by pests, and
      it does not cover a new problem that is different from the one you hired us
      for.
    </p>
    <p>
      You will sometimes see competitors advertise an unlimited return-visit
      promise with no terms attached anywhere on the site. A promise with no
      stated conditions cannot be enforced as written, which means in practice it
      is granted at the company's discretion rather than owed to you. We would
      rather publish conditions you can hold us to.
    </p>

    <h2>What it covers in practice</h2>
    <p>
      On an active recurring program, if a pest covered by that program returns
      between scheduled visits, you call us and we come back at no additional
      charge. There is no cap on the number of return visits within the program
      period and no argument about whether it has been too soon.
    </p>
    <p>
      On a one-time treatment, the guarantee runs for the period stated on your
      service agreement for that specific job, because a single visit for a
      specific problem is a different commitment from an ongoing program. That
      period is written on the agreement before you sign it rather than being
      referenced vaguely somewhere else.
    </p>
    <p>
      Exclusion and repair work is covered on its own terms. A well-installed
      exclusion does not wear out the way a treatment does, so what we stand
      behind there is the workmanship — fastenings, edges and seals — rather than
      a re-treatment cycle.
    </p>

    <h2>What we need from you</h2>
    <p>
      Two things, and they are the reason the "customer cooperation" clause below
      exists. The first is access: we cannot re-service a crawlspace we cannot
      get into, or an area that is blocked on the day. The second is preparation,
      which matters enormously on bed bug work in particular, where a treatment
      performed against an unprepared room is close to wasted and we would rather
      reschedule than pretend otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is also a third thing that is not a condition but is worth saying: if
      we tell you that a gutter, a vent screen or a door sweep is the actual cause
      of the problem, the guarantee does not substitute for fixing it. We will
      keep coming back, and the pests will keep coming back with us.
    </p>

    <h2>General terms and conditions</h2>
    {terms.map(([h, body]) => (
      <>
        <h3>{h}</h3>
        <p>{body}</p>
      </>
    ))}

    <h3>Why we publish all of this</h3>
    <p>
      Most guarantee pages in this industry are a paragraph of reassurance and a
      phone number. That is a marketing asset, not a commitment, and it works
      precisely because nobody expects to be able to check it.
    </p>
    <p>
      We publish the conditions because a guarantee with no published conditions
      cannot be enforced by the customer, only granted by the company. If you can
      read what we owe you, you can hold us to it — and if we ever fail to honor
      what is on this page, you have the page.
    </p>

    <h3>How to make a claim</h3>
    <p>
      Call or text us and say what came back and when. There is no form, no
      claim number and no waiting period. We will schedule the return visit the
      same way we scheduled the original one, and there is no charge for it on a
      covered program.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we disagree about whether something is covered — usually because a new
      and different pest has appeared, or because the original problem was tied to
      a repair that has not been made — we will tell you why in plain language and
      quote the work separately rather than quietly declining.
    </p>

    <h3>Recurring programs and cancellation</h3>
    <p>
      Recurring programs exist because pest pressure is recurring, not because we
      want you locked in. There is no multi-year term, no early termination
      penalty buried in a schedule, and no requirement to justify a cancellation.
      The notice period is stated on your service agreement, and it is short.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you cancel mid-program, guarantee coverage runs to the end of the period
      you have already paid for rather than stopping on the day you call. We are
      not going to argue about a re-service in the last three weeks of a program
      you have decided not to renew.
    </p>

    <h3>If something goes wrong on our side</h3>
    <p>
      Occasionally a treatment does not perform, a technician misses something, or
      a scheduled visit does not happen when it should have. The guarantee covers
      the first of those; the other two are just us getting it wrong, and the
      answer is the same — tell us and we will make it right without requiring you
      to argue the point.
    </p>

    <h3>Why no contract</h3>
    <p>
      The long-term contract is standard in this industry, and its real function
      is retention rather than service quality. A company confident in its work
      does not need a termination penalty to keep customers, and a company that
      needs one has told you something about its work.
    </p>
    <p>
      We would rather earn the next visit each time. It means we lose customers
      who could have been held in place by paperwork, and it means the ones who
      stay are there because the service is worth staying for.
    </p>

    <h3>Disclaimer</h3>
    <p>
      These terms summarize the guarantee attached to our service programs. Where
      this page and your signed service agreement differ, the service agreement
      governs.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Cta market="Whatcom County" />
</BaseLayout>
